# p_4e8a — Couple: one WFH, one daily commuter; desk item not always at desk; work-kit item occasionally in-house (fork of p_a7f3)

Two adults live here. Partner A works from home every weekday (09:00–17:00, primarily at the desk, receptacle_12). Partner B commutes to an office, leaving around 07:30 and returning around 17:30 on weekdays. The keys (object_2) and bag (object_35) at receptacle_11 are Partner A's set; Partner B's keys and work bag are out during the workday.

What changed from the parent (p_a7f3) and why: the object_24 claim went against twice since the last call, and the per-object log shows object_24 was sighted at receptacle_19 on day 9 at 15:00 — a weekday midday look that found it at the shared workspace rather than the desk. Over the full nine-day window, weekday 9–17 h looks at receptacle_12 found object_24 three times and found nothing two times (60 % hit rate). "Almost always" overstates the reliability; "usually" matches the data. I have downgraded object_24's all-day block from almost_always to usually. Partner A appears to move the item to receptacle_19 (a secondary work surface) for part of the day, perhaps to reference materials or switch tasks.

Second change: object_33's weekday out-block is downgraded from "usually" to "sometimes." On day 8 at 12:00 the robot found object_33 at receptacle_20, in the house, contradicting the "out with Partner B" prediction. The per-object log shows object_33 at receptacle_11 on only 3 of 8 sighted days, with five distinct receptacles. It is a shared item that Partner B takes on some days but leaves on others.

